BT /F1 10 Tf 50 720 Td (IN THE MADRAS HIGH COURT \(MADURAI BENCH\)
CASE NO: Crl.O.P.\(MD\) No. 6214 of 2026
CNR NUMBER: HCMD010891232026
YEAR: 2026

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Justice G.R. Swaminathan

PARTIES:
S. Muthulakshmi
... Petitioner\(s\) / Appellant\(s\)
Versus
Home Secretary, Government of Tamil Nadu & Superintendent of Police, Thoothukudi
... Respondent\(s\)

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Constitution of India, Code of Criminal Procedure 1973

SECTIONS & PROVISIONS:
Article 21, Article 22, CrPC Section 176\(1A\)

KEY TOPICS & ISSUES:
Custodial Torture, Human Rights Violation, D.K. Basu Guidelines, Public Law Remedy, Strict Liability

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTS OF THE CASE:
Petitioner's son suffered multiple fractures and renal failure while detained illegally for 3 days in police custody.

2. ISSUES FRAMED:
Whether public law compensation under Article 226 is available for custodial torture independent of private civil suit?

3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:
Custodial violence is an assault on human dignity and democracy; constitutional courts have duty to award strict liability compensation under Article 21.

4. FINAL ORDER:
Petition Allowed; Compensation of Rs. 15 Lakhs awarded for custodial torture and CB-CID inquiry directed.

Ordered and decreed accordingly.

Hon'ble Justice G.R. Swaminathan
Madras High Court \(Madurai Bench\)
[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]
) Tj ET
